### Budget API Testing

### Notes
### ============================================
# How to use this file:
# 1. Get a token: log in via the gateway (POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
#    or /api/auth/demo), then call any gateway-proxied route — the edge
#    mints the internal JWT per request. To call :6969 directly, copy the
#    downstream Authorization value from a proxied request and paste it
#    below as @jwt (5-minute TTL).
# 2. Run any request - Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}} is sent automatically.
#
# Auth: every route except /health, /, /websocket and
# /api/budget/priority-groups requires a gateway-created internal JWT.
# X-User-ID is NOT accepted from the wire (spoofing returns 401).
#
# Endpoints implemented (canonical prefix /api/budget/* for ALL verbs):
# - Expense Categories: full CRUD (soft delete via is_active)
# - Income Categories: full CRUD (soft delete via is_active)
# - Tags: full CRUD (hard delete) + tag associations for expenses/incomes
# - Expenses: full CRUD + search + skip + check-skipped + tag management
# - Incomes: full CRUD + skip + check-skipped + occurrences + tag management
# - Priority Groups: hardcoded reference data (need/want/savings)
# - Budget Remaining: current month income - expenses (no query params)
# - Stats: summary, trends, category-breakdown, savings-rate (optional start_date/end_date)
# - Analysis: 50/30/20 breakdown by priority (optional start_date/end_date)
# - Velocity: average monthly spending (REQUIRED start_date + end_date, else 400)
# - Forecast: upcoming recurring expenses (no query params)
# - Current Total Money: total income - total expenses, lifetime (NO date params)
# - Month-over-Month: combined monthly trends (send start_date + end_date; SQL requires both)
# - Recurring Expenses: full CRUD
# - Recurring Incomes: full CRUD
# - Export/Import: JSON backup with ID remapping
# - Admin Backfill: per-user legacy inline-rule conversion (admin scope only;
#   POST only, ?dry_run=true counts without mutating, ?user_id targets anyone)
# - Health: pgxpool ping + connection stats


### Health Check

GET {{baseUrl}}/health HTTP/1.1

